Text content with Unicode spaces (NBSP U+00A0, ideographic U+3000)
alongside an inline <code> sibling, exercising the full text+atom render
path end-to-end. wsnorm's whitespace model is ASCII-only (see
whitespace/element_baseline.txtar); these are non-collapsible CONTENT
runes, not word-gap whitespace, and must reach render.golden byte-for-
byte, both in a plain Text node and adjacent to a component interp.
-- input.gsx --
package views

component UnicodeText(name string) {
	<p>Reading <code>{name}</code> covers 10 km basics and 日本　語 notes today.</p>
}
-- invoke --
UnicodeText("the guide")
-- diagnostics.golden --
-- render.golden --
<p>Reading <code>the guide</code> covers 10 km basics and 日本　語 notes today.</p>
-- generated.x.go.golden --
